<!--
  Photos in assets/img/projects/ are hand-drawn placeholders (chip + system
  pair per project) standing in until real die/board photos are ready. Swap
  the *-chip.svg / *-system.svg files at the same paths; no markup change
  needed. Projects below are drawn from the lab's most recent publications
  (see _bibliography/papers.bib) as a stand-in "latest projects" list —
  swap in dedicated project write-ups once available. Layout: small
  side-by-side chip/system thumbnails on the left, more room for text
  (venue + motivation + highlights) on the right, so longer descriptions
  don't end up as a single cramped line under two large images.
-->
{% capture proj_thumb_sizes %}(min-width: {{ site.max_width }}) 280px, (min-width: 768px) 23vw, 45vw{% endcapture %}
<div class="row row-cols-1 g-4 mt-2">
  <div class="col">
    <div class="card hoverable">
      <div class="card-body project-card-body">
        <div class="row">
          <div class="col-md-4 proj-media">
            <div class="row g-2">
              <div class="col-sm-6">
                {% include figure.liquid path="assets/img/projects/hoop-chip.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" alt="HOOP converter chip photo" sizes=proj_thumb_sizes %}
                <p class="caption mt-1"><span class="lang-en">Chip</span><span class="lang-zh">芯片图</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="col-sm-6">
                {% include figure.liquid path="assets/img/projects/hoop-system.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" alt="HOOP converter system photo" sizes=proj_thumb_sizes %}
                <p class="caption mt-1"><span class="lang-en">System</span><span class="lang-zh">系统图</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-8 proj-text">
            <h4 class="mt-3 mt-md-0">
              <span class="lang-en">HOOP: A Scalable Hybrid DC-DC Converter Ring for High-Performance Computing</span>
              <span class="lang-zh">HOOP：面向高性能计算的可扩展混合 DC-DC 变换器环</span>
              <span>(ISSCC 2025)</span>
              <a href="{{ '/assets/pdf/hoop-isscc-2025.pdf' | relative_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Read project paper (PDF)"
                >[PDF]</a
              >
            </h4>

            <p class="lang-en">
              <strong>Motivation.</strong> AI processors require large currents at low supply voltages. As more converter phases are connected in
              parallel, coordinating current sharing and maintaining light-load efficiency become increasingly difficult.
            </p>
            <p class="lang-zh">
              <strong>研究背景。</strong>AI
              处理器需要低电压、大电流供电。随着并联供电相数增加，相间均流与轻载效率管理的复杂度也随之上升，限制了供电系统的扩展。
            </p>
            <p class="lang-en">
              <strong>Approach &amp; Results.</strong> HOOP links hybrid converter cells through a power ring for inherent current balancing and a
              back ring for phase shedding. The ring architecture supports parallel expansion while adjusting the active phase count to load demand,
              addressing both current sharing at heavy load and efficiency management at light load.
            </p>
            <p class="lang-zh">
              <strong>技术与成果。</strong>HOOP
              将混合变换单元连接成用于自动均流的功率环，并引入支持切相的回环。环形架构支持多相并联扩展，同时根据负载调整工作相数，兼顾重载时的电流分配与轻载时的效率管理，为高性能计算提供可扩展供电方案。
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="col">
    <div class="card hoverable">
      <div class="card-body project-card-body">
        <div class="row">
          <div class="col-md-4 proj-media">
            <div class="row g-2">
              <div class="col-sm-6">
                <img
                  src="{{ '/assets/img/projects/robot-cable-chip.png' | relative_url }}"
                  class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1"
                  alt="Robot power cable chip photo"
                >
                <p class="caption mt-1"><span class="lang-en">Chip</span><span class="lang-zh">芯片图</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="col-sm-6">
                <img
                  src="{{ '/assets/img/projects/robot-cable-system.png' | relative_url }}"
                  class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1"
                  alt="Robot power cable system photo"
                >
                <p class="caption mt-1"><span class="lang-en">System</span><span class="lang-zh">系统图</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-8 proj-text">
            <h4 class="mt-3 mt-md-0">
              <span class="lang-en"
                >Bi-Directional Dual-Path Boost–Buck Hybrid Converter for High-Voltage Power Transmission Cable in Humanoid Robots</span
              >
              <span class="lang-zh">面向人形机器人高压电源传输线缆的双向双路径升降压混合变换器</span>
              <span>(JSSC 2025)</span>
              <a
                href="{{ '/assets/pdf/robot-cable-jssc-2025.pdf' | relative_url }}"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener"
                aria-label="Read project paper (PDF)"
                >[PDF]</a
              >
            </h4>

            <p class="lang-en">
              <strong>Motivation.</strong> Power must travel from a torso-mounted battery to actuators throughout a humanoid robot. High cable
              currents increase conduction loss and require heavier wiring, making power distribution a constraint on lightweight design.
            </p>
            <p class="lang-zh">
              <strong>研究背景。</strong
              >人形机器人的电池通常位于躯干，而执行器分布在四肢。大电流传输带来的线缆损耗和粗重导线，使供电网络成为机器人轻量化设计的重要制约。
            </p>
            <p class="lang-en">
              <strong>Approach &amp; Results.</strong> A bidirectional dual-path boost–buck architecture uses a 48 V transmission bus, reuses cable
              parasitic inductance for power conversion, and aligns switching phases to reduce cable-current ripple. The ISSCC 2025 prototype achieves
              up to 45 W transmission power and 96.7% peak chip efficiency at 16.5 W output, reducing the need for a separate bulky power inductor.
            </p>
            <p class="lang-zh">
              <strong>技术与成果。</strong>采用双向双路径升降压架构，以 48 V
              母线传输功率，复用线缆寄生电感参与能量转换，并通过相位对齐降低线缆电流纹波。ISSCC 2025 原型最大传输功率为 45 W，在 16.5 W
              输出时芯片峰值效率达 96.7%，减少对额外大体积功率电感的依赖。
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="col">
    <div class="card hoverable">
      <div class="card-body project-card-body">
        <div class="row">
          <div class="col-md-4 proj-media">
            <div class="row g-2">
              <div class="col-sm-6">
                {% include figure.liquid path="assets/img/projects/usb-pd-chip.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" alt="USB PD cable chip photo" sizes=proj_thumb_sizes %}
                <p class="caption mt-1"><span class="lang-en">Chip</span><span class="lang-zh">芯片图</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="col-sm-6">
                {% include figure.liquid path="assets/img/projects/usb-pd-system.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" alt="USB PD cable system photo" sizes=proj_thumb_sizes %}
                <p class="caption mt-1"><span class="lang-en">System</span><span class="lang-zh">系统图</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-8 proj-text">
            <h4 class="mt-3 mt-md-0">
              <span class="lang-en">A Bidirectional USB Power Delivery Voltage-Regulating Cable</span>
              <span class="lang-zh">双向 USB 电源传输稳压线缆</span>
              <span>(JSSC 2025)</span>
              <a
                href="{{ '/assets/pdf/usb-pd-cable-jssc-2025.pdf' | relative_url }}"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener"
                aria-label="Read project paper (PDF)"
                >[PDF]</a
              >
            </h4>

            <p class="lang-en">
              <strong>Motivation.</strong> Fast charging concentrates power-conversion heat inside compact devices. Moving voltage regulation into the
              USB cable offers a way to reduce the thermal burden on the device while supporting power exchange between devices.
            </p>
            <p class="lang-zh">
              <strong>研究背景。</strong>快充功率提升会加重紧凑型设备内部的散热负担。将电压调节功能移至 USB
              线缆，可把部分功率转换及其热量从设备内部移出，同时支持设备之间的电能互供。
            </p>
            <p class="lang-en">
              <strong>Approach &amp; Results.</strong> The voltage-regulating cable integrates the converter and passive components into the USB
              connector, moving conversion heat outside the device. Bidirectional regulation supports adapter-to-device charging and device-to-device
              power exchange. The 42 W ISSCC prototype achieves 95.1% peak converter efficiency at 22.8 W, excluding cable loss, with a reported power
              density of 3.17 W/mm².
            </p>
            <p class="lang-zh">
              <strong>技术与成果。</strong>将变换器与无源器件集成到 USB
              连接器中，把功率转换及其热量从设备内部移至线缆，支持适配器向设备充电及设备间双向互供。42 W ISSCC 原型在 22.8 W 时达到 95.1%
              的变换器峰值效率（不含线缆损耗），报告的功率密度为 3.17 W/mm²。
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="col">
    <div class="card hoverable">
      <div class="card-body project-card-body">
        <div class="row">
          <div class="col-md-4 proj-media">
            <div class="row g-2">
              <div class="col-sm-6">
                {% include figure.liquid path="assets/img/projects/lscb-chip.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" alt="Ladder buck converter chip photo" sizes=proj_thumb_sizes %}
                <p class="caption mt-1"><span class="lang-en">Chip</span><span class="lang-zh">芯片图</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="col-sm-6">
                {% include figure.liquid path="assets/img/projects/lscb-system.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" alt="Ladder buck converter system photo" sizes=proj_thumb_sizes %}
                <p class="caption mt-1"><span class="lang-en">System</span><span class="lang-zh">系统图</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-8 proj-text">
            <h4 class="mt-3 mt-md-0">
              <span class="lang-en">A 2D-Extendable 48V-1V Ladder-Series-Capacitor Buck Converter for Computing Power Delivery</span>
              <span class="lang-zh">面向计算供电的二维可扩展 48V-1V 阶梯式串联电容降压变换器</span>
              <span>(VLSI Symp. 2026)</span>
              <a
                href="{{ '/assets/pdf/ladder-buck-vlsi-2026.pdf' | relative_url }}"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener"
                aria-label="Read project paper (PDF)"
                >[PDF]</a
              >
            </h4>

            <p class="lang-en">
              <strong>Motivation.</strong> Computing loads require a large step-down ratio from a 48 V distribution bus to a 1 V supply. A scalable
              architecture must accommodate the input voltage while increasing output-current capability for growing compute demand.
            </p>
            <p class="lang-zh">
              <strong>研究背景。</strong>计算负载需要将 48 V 配电母线转换为约 1 V
              的供电电压。面对持续增长的算力需求，供电架构既要适应高输入电压，也要能够扩展输出电流能力。
            </p>
            <p class="lang-en">
              <strong>Approach &amp; Results.</strong> The ladder-series-capacitor buck architecture combines capacitive voltage division with
              inductive power conversion to achieve 48 V-to-1 V conversion. Two-dimensional extension scales the input-voltage and output-current
              capabilities of the power cells, providing an architecture for high step-down ratios and growing computing loads.
            </p>
            <p class="lang-zh">
              <strong>技术与成果。</strong>采用阶梯式串联电容降压架构，将电容分压与电感功率转换相结合，实现 48 V 至 1 V
              的大降压比转换。通过功率单元的二维扩展，分别适应输入电压与输出电流能力的扩展需求，为持续增长的计算负载提供可扩展供电架构。
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="col">
    <div class="card hoverable">
      <div class="card-body project-card-body">
        <div class="row">
          <div class="col-md-4 proj-media">
            <div class="row g-2">
              <div class="col-sm-6">
                {% include figure.liquid path="assets/img/projects/lidar-chip.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" alt="LiDAR laser diode driver chip photo" sizes=proj_thumb_sizes %}
                <p class="caption mt-1"><span class="lang-en">Chip</span><span class="lang-zh">芯片图</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="col-sm-6">
                {% include figure.liquid path="assets/img/projects/lidar-system.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" alt="LiDAR laser diode driver system photo" sizes=proj_thumb_sizes %}
                <p class="caption mt-1"><span class="lang-en">System</span><span class="lang-zh">系统图</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="col-md-8 proj-text">
            <h4 class="mt-3 mt-md-0">
              <span class="lang-en">A Double Pulse Overlapping Laser Diode Driver With Minimum 100-ps Pulse for LiDAR System</span>
              <span class="lang-zh">面向激光雷达系统的双脉冲交叠式激光二极管驱动器</span>
              <span>(JSSC 2025)</span>
              <a
                href="{{ '/assets/pdf/lidar-driver-jssc-2025.pdf' | relative_url }}"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener"
                aria-label="Read project paper (PDF)"
                >[PDF]</a
              >
            </h4>

            <p class="lang-en">
              <strong>Motivation.</strong> Direct time-of-flight LiDAR needs short laser pulses to distinguish closely spaced returns. The laser
              driver must generate these pulses despite switching-speed and interconnect-parasitic constraints.
            </p>
            <p class="lang-zh">
              <strong>研究背景。</strong
              >直接飞行时间（dToF）激光雷达需要短激光脉冲来分辨时间上相近的回波。驱动器必须在开关速度和互连寄生参数的约束下，实现超短脉冲激光发射。
            </p>
            <p class="lang-en">
              <strong>Approach &amp; Results.</strong> The double pulse overlapping scheme sets the laser-driving window through the overlap of two
              control pulses, generating laser pulses shorter than the control signals themselves. A minimum pulse width of 100 ps demonstrates
              sub-nanosecond pulse generation for high-resolution direct time-of-flight LiDAR transmitters.
            </p>
            <p class="lang-zh">
              <strong>技术与成果。</strong
              >采用双脉冲交叠（DPO）方案，以两路控制脉冲的交叠时间确定激光驱动窗口，产生比控制信号本身更短的激光脉冲。实现最小 100 ps
              脉宽，验证亚纳秒激光脉冲产生能力，为高分辨率直接飞行时间（dToF）激光雷达发射端提供驱动方案。
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
